# ── Visual fidelity ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# What is TRACKED is deliberate. The baselines, the DOM signatures and the HARs under
# tests/visual/ are the contract every page is measured against — they come from the prototype
# and nowhere else, so they belong in review like any other specification. design-reference/ and
# its _rendered/ captures are tracked for the same reason: _rendered/ is what each screen is ported
# from (tests/visual/README.md §5), and a port is not reviewable if its source is not in the tree.
#
# Only per-run output is ignored.
/tests/visual/artifacts
/tests/visual/test-results
/tests/visual/playwright-report
/tests/visual/report.html
/tests/visual/capture-manifest.json
